WEBVTT

00:21.200 --> 00:22.830
Get away from me!

01:23.950 --> 01:32.690
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

02:15.670 --> 02:20.510
<b>Episode Forty-Four
Brown Bear Man</b>

02:23.580 --> 02:28.040
Seeing these Ainu cise makes me feel 
like we're really back in Hokkaido.

02:28.300 --> 02:31.710
Yeah, we're back to Hokkaido at last.

02:37.210 --> 02:40.210
So, now what?

02:40.530 --> 02:43.890
You got a plan to help us find 
the gold all by ourselves?

02:45.270 --> 02:49.040
Am I right in thinking our only 
choice is to steal the skins

02:49.040 --> 02:50.480
from both Hijikata and Tsurumi?

02:50.750 --> 02:54.240
We'll lead the two sides right to each other...
and get the skins while they fight!

02:54.670 --> 02:56.700
Two birds with one stone, right?

02:58.890 --> 03:01.320
Easier said than done.

03:01.320 --> 03:06.790
Hey, Nispa, any easy ways to 
make some cash for our travels?

03:07.450 --> 03:12.450
There's a kotan to the south that's 
asked for help slaying a wenkamuy.

03:12.450 --> 03:15.750
A wenkamuy? Isn't that a 
bear that's killed someone?

03:15.750 --> 03:16.550
Yes.

03:17.070 --> 03:22.260
Supposedly everyone who was killed 
was looking for gold in the river.

03:22.260 --> 03:23.450
Gold?

03:23.450 --> 03:27.580
And now everyone's too scared of 
the wenkamuy to go near the river.

03:27.980 --> 03:30.100
Are there still rivers with gold in them?

03:30.100 --> 03:32.520
I had no luck when I tried.

03:32.520 --> 03:39.860
<b>Present
 Location</b>

03:32.520 --> 03:39.860
<b>Uryu River</b>

03:32.520 --> 03:39.860
<b>Abashiri</b>

03:32.890 --> 03:34.400
The rumors are that

03:34.400 --> 03:39.860
there's a man who pans for gold at the 
Uryu River who's been getting rich lately.

03:40.150 --> 03:45.180
If you want money, pan for gold. 
Just watch out for the wenkamuy.

03:45.180 --> 03:48.990
Supposedly, he made 50 yen in a day.

03:49.720 --> 03:51.320
<i>A whole 50 yen?!</i>

04:12.760 --> 04:16.850
Help me! Help me!

04:16.850 --> 04:21.070
Dad! Brother Taka! Brother Jiro!

04:21.340 --> 04:25.570
Hurry! I'm slipping! I'm done for!

04:25.790 --> 04:27.090
Somebody...

04:29.300 --> 04:30.580
We made it!

04:36.450 --> 04:38.650
Thank you.

04:39.260 --> 04:41.090
You saved my life.

04:41.090 --> 04:43.260
You've got an injury there, are you okay?

04:43.260 --> 04:46.550
Oh, this is from a little while ago...

04:47.690 --> 04:49.720
<i>He's so kind!</i>

04:49.930 --> 04:50.990
Heita!

04:50.990 --> 04:52.140
I'm so glad you're okay.

04:52.500 --> 04:53.950
Brother Taka!

04:53.950 --> 04:56.590
You looking for gold?

04:57.430 --> 05:00.480
Yes... I'm impressed you could tell.

05:00.740 --> 05:04.000
We came to pan for gold ourselves.

05:04.000 --> 05:06.330
We heard there was a lot 
here in the Uryu River.

05:10.190 --> 05:12.450
Oh, I see!

05:12.890 --> 05:15.560
There's a lot here still, if you look for it!

05:18.460 --> 05:22.520
Oh my, what an unusual group.

05:22.520 --> 05:24.330
They must be having such fun together!

05:24.330 --> 05:27.020
How are you all related?

05:27.470 --> 05:29.970
I see one of you is even 
from a foreign country.

05:29.970 --> 05:32.880
We're, uh... buddies?

05:32.880 --> 05:34.930
No, just nobodies.

05:34.930 --> 05:37.350
Noriko, get back to the hut!

05:39.270 --> 05:43.770
We use a glass box to look at the river 
bottom and in cracks in the rocks.

05:44.490 --> 05:47.900
That's why this method 
is called glass digging.

05:48.660 --> 05:52.650
Then you use this metal scraper to 
dig out the gold from the cracks.

05:52.650 --> 05:55.700
It's an easy way to find big chunks of gold.

05:56.050 --> 06:00.550
What you're trying to do is called panning.

06:00.550 --> 06:03.640
It's hard to pick the 
right spot to do panning.

06:03.640 --> 06:05.720
I knew it.

06:05.720 --> 06:08.760
I tried it once before 
and didn't get anywhere.

06:09.080 --> 06:11.560
Could you tell me where to start?

06:11.560 --> 06:12.720
Please?

06:12.720 --> 06:19.140
Hmm... in this area, you might 
want to try under that big rock.

06:25.890 --> 06:27.900
I can't do this anymore!

06:28.190 --> 06:30.730
Asirpa-chan! Hot water!

06:35.350 --> 06:36.730
Heaven...

06:36.730 --> 06:38.790
At this time of year,

06:38.790 --> 06:41.880
you can only look for gold for around four 
hours during the hottest part of the day.

06:41.880 --> 06:46.140
And panning's the least 
efficient way to do it.

06:46.140 --> 06:50.070
I should've known we wouldn't get anywhere.

06:50.070 --> 06:55.260
That story about someone making 50 yen in 
a day at the Uryu River was all lies, then?

06:56.910 --> 06:59.280
It's true.

06:59.280 --> 07:01.770
Because I was the one who did it.

07:02.850 --> 07:05.150
Heita! You keep your mouth shut!

07:05.150 --> 07:08.850
They saved my life, 
so I'm going to tell them.

07:09.220 --> 07:11.360
Do you know what I mean when I say "white"?

07:11.360 --> 07:13.270
What's "white"?

07:13.270 --> 07:14.830
I'll show you.

07:15.310 --> 07:17.040
Here.

07:17.380 --> 07:21.400
Gold hunters call gold "red."

07:21.400 --> 07:26.220
And this, which we call "white," 
is always found mixed in with it.

07:26.220 --> 07:29.050
It's actually something called platinum.

07:29.450 --> 07:32.040
It's very hard!

07:32.040 --> 07:35.450
It's resistant to heat and acid can't touch it!

07:35.450 --> 07:39.060
Jewelers don't like it because 
it damages their tools.

07:39.060 --> 07:41.810
If it's mixed in with the gold,
 the gold's worth less.

07:42.020 --> 07:45.520
So until now you've had 
to pick it out by hand.

07:45.520 --> 07:47.570
And it takes forever!

07:48.010 --> 07:51.200
The white is only found in Hokkaido,

07:51.200 --> 07:55.010
and the Uryu River has an 
exceptionally large amount.

07:55.010 --> 07:56.530
Huh? Then that's no good.

07:56.530 --> 08:01.810
But get this. Now there are people 
who'll pay a high price for it!

08:01.810 --> 08:03.830
Three yen for one monme!

08:04.980 --> 08:08.250
That's almost as much as gold's worth!

08:08.500 --> 08:10.070
There was this guy who ran an arms factory

08:10.070 --> 08:12.340
that had to shut down after 
the Russo-Japanese War ended,

08:12.340 --> 08:16.140
so he decided to be the first 
Japanese man to make fountain pens.

08:16.460 --> 08:20.300
He realized that the hard, 
friction-resistant metal on the edge

08:20.300 --> 08:26.270
of the fountain pens from 
overseas was actually platinum.

08:26.270 --> 08:31.420
And then he realized he could get 
his own platinum from Hokkaido!

08:31.420 --> 08:35.280
We thought the white was worthless, but now 
it's getting more valuable by the day!

08:35.780 --> 08:38.700
Of course, people from 
outside Japan want it, too.

08:38.940 --> 08:42.100
Until now, we just threw the white away!

08:42.100 --> 08:44.670
We just tossed the stuff back 
into every river in Hokkaido!

08:44.670 --> 08:48.000
This is the start of a second gold rush!

08:56.310 --> 08:57.920
Him again!

08:57.920 --> 08:59.260
The same bear...

09:00.070 --> 09:00.940
Where?

09:00.940 --> 09:01.890
Where is he?

09:02.100 --> 09:03.640
Over there! Look!

09:03.960 --> 09:05.390
He's staring at us.

09:06.680 --> 09:08.530
He disappeared.

09:09.890 --> 09:12.150
But he's getting closer...

09:12.640 --> 09:15.280
Yesterday he was further away.

09:16.090 --> 09:18.240
That's a wenkamuy.

09:23.520 --> 09:25.130
Asirpa-san? Well?

09:25.970 --> 09:27.300
See any footprints?

09:27.300 --> 09:29.000
No. Not a thing.

09:29.000 --> 09:31.520
So it got away by moving 
over the bamboo grass?

09:32.430 --> 09:33.490
I'm not so sure.

09:37.850 --> 09:39.640
A chakchak kamuy?

09:39.640 --> 09:45.850
If there was a bear nearby, it would cry, 
"Chakchak!" and try to lead us to it.

09:46.880 --> 09:48.060
But it's quiet.

09:48.850 --> 09:50.570
Here!

09:50.570 --> 09:53.070
This is the spot.

09:53.400 --> 09:56.190
I bet you could find lots of platinum here.

09:56.190 --> 09:59.980
You could get more than 10 monme in a day.

10:01.070 --> 10:04.580
We'll split it evenly with you.

10:05.040 --> 10:07.680
More than 50 yen! In a day!

10:07.680 --> 10:11.380
That sounds a lot better than risking 
having a bear rip our faces off!

10:11.380 --> 10:15.880
That's why everyone stopped hunting and 
dug for gold, and the rivers got polluted!

10:15.880 --> 10:19.140
Master Heita, thank you 
for your kind tutelage!

10:23.870 --> 10:26.600
That tobacco case... That was 
made by an Ainu, right?

10:27.800 --> 10:34.340
Oh, this? I once hunted gold with the Ainu.

10:34.340 --> 10:36.570
We got to be friends, and they gave it to me.

10:36.880 --> 10:38.010
I see.

10:38.010 --> 10:40.280
That's how you know the word wenkamuy.

10:40.500 --> 10:45.160
When I was a child, the Ainu told 
me a story about the wenkamuy.

10:45.160 --> 10:49.790
It was so scary I couldn't sleep.

10:50.190 --> 10:53.030
I was so, so, <i>so</i> scared...

10:53.030 --> 10:55.030
I peed my bed every night!

10:55.030 --> 10:57.380
Poor young Heita!

10:57.380 --> 11:01.640
So scared, so scared, so scared, so scared...

11:01.980 --> 11:04.720
We've heard about the wenkamuy, too.

11:04.720 --> 11:06.970
They say it's attacked a lot 
of people around the Uryu River

11:06.970 --> 11:08.360
who are hunting for gold.

11:08.360 --> 11:10.400
Don't worry!

11:10.400 --> 11:13.610
We have a dedicated bear-hunting 
specialist with us today.

11:13.610 --> 11:16.880
So just focus on finding that platinum!

11:16.880 --> 11:19.200
You said it was getting closer, right?

11:20.150 --> 11:23.160
How long has it been 
wandering around here?

11:23.160 --> 11:25.160
For years.

11:30.180 --> 11:31.830
Are you drawing?

11:32.710 --> 11:33.920
Is it fun?

11:34.360 --> 11:37.550
Hey, would you draw me?

11:38.130 --> 11:40.550
Draw. Me.

11:41.940 --> 11:43.550
Come here.

11:44.560 --> 11:46.560
It's cold. You can draw inside.

11:47.270 --> 11:48.680
Come inside...

11:56.090 --> 11:57.820
Make me look pretty.

12:01.360 --> 12:04.070
Do you like my body?

12:10.000 --> 12:11.720
Again...

12:11.720 --> 12:13.460
I threw it away!

12:14.640 --> 12:16.590
Noriko, what are you doing?

12:17.170 --> 12:19.610
Well, I was bored.

12:19.610 --> 12:23.430
That doesn't mean you should be taking 
your clothes off for a man you just met!

12:23.670 --> 12:26.140
I'm not interested in him.

12:26.140 --> 12:29.390
I just wanted to have a picture so I 
could remember how beautiful I was.

12:29.880 --> 12:33.550
If I spend the rest of my life watching 
you hunt gold here on this mountain,

12:33.550 --> 12:36.400
I'll be an old lady before you know it.

12:37.060 --> 12:38.310
I'm sorry.

12:38.310 --> 12:39.500
All right.

12:39.500 --> 12:40.890
It won't be for much longer.

12:43.710 --> 12:47.790
Once I make a ton of money off the white, 
I'll go to Tokyo and open a business.

12:51.420 --> 12:54.090
Huh? Hey, where's Master Heita?

12:54.430 --> 12:56.150
Did he wander off?

12:56.520 --> 12:59.690
That's dangerous! There's a 
man-eating bear on the loose!

12:59.690 --> 13:03.220
Asirpa-chan! Master Heita's gone missing!

13:03.220 --> 13:05.050
Can you go look for him?

13:05.520 --> 13:10.170
If he gets eaten, we won't get any money!

13:10.170 --> 13:12.540
If there really is a bear, maybe.

13:17.390 --> 13:18.700
Hey, mister.

13:22.760 --> 13:24.870
Over here. Come here.

13:25.220 --> 13:31.830
Aren't those your binoculars on 
top of that monkey chair mushroom?

13:32.170 --> 13:34.710
It was probably Noriko playing a prank.

13:46.460 --> 13:48.640
That was an amappo. That was close.

13:49.160 --> 13:52.370
Trees trapped with an amappo 
will have holes made in the bark

13:52.370 --> 13:54.140
or other ways to recognize them.

13:54.500 --> 13:56.410
Make sure to remember that.

13:56.950 --> 13:59.860
Somebody set it here to catch deer, probably.

13:59.860 --> 14:03.360
The brown bears are still all 
in their dens, after all.

14:03.880 --> 14:07.770
I looked around in a wider 
area than where Heita was.

14:07.770 --> 14:11.530
But I didn't see a single sign of a 
matakarip that didn't hibernate in winter.

14:12.230 --> 14:16.550
Why did Heita lie about seeing a bear?

14:17.370 --> 14:19.620
Sugimoto, look!

14:21.850 --> 14:23.450
Asirpa-san!

14:23.450 --> 14:25.340
The bear's over there!

14:25.640 --> 14:26.970
We saw it, too!

14:26.970 --> 14:29.780
Master Heita was right! It's close!

14:29.780 --> 14:32.890
We need to protect Master 
Heita from the wenkamuy!

14:35.990 --> 14:40.900
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

14:42.430 --> 14:43.860
That's strange.

14:44.150 --> 14:46.580
I know it was around here.

14:46.580 --> 14:48.380
Stop walking around!

14:48.380 --> 14:50.860
I won't be able to tell your 
prints from the bear's!

14:51.170 --> 14:55.580
There's no way a brown bear 
wouldn't leave footprints.

14:55.860 --> 14:56.810
Right.

14:56.810 --> 15:00.500
We'll defeat the bear. Shiraishi, 
you look for Master Heita.

15:00.500 --> 15:02.000
Take Mister Hood with you.

15:02.000 --> 15:03.130
Roger!

15:08.050 --> 15:11.050
Dad... Brother Jiro...

15:15.560 --> 15:17.280
Is someone praying?

15:18.480 --> 15:21.960
Buddha protect me... Buddha protect me...

15:22.510 --> 15:31.250
Buddha protect me... Buddha protect me...

15:37.380 --> 15:38.410
Are you hurt?

15:38.410 --> 15:42.720
Heita! Taka-san was... Taka-san was...

15:45.610 --> 15:46.730
No!

15:47.050 --> 15:48.420
I'm sorry!

15:48.420 --> 15:50.580
Don't tell Brother Taka.

15:50.580 --> 15:52.680
He'll hit me again!

15:58.280 --> 16:00.180
It's your fault, Sister Noriko!

16:04.900 --> 16:06.890
What's wrong, Master Heita?

16:06.890 --> 16:07.980
Did you see the bear?

16:07.980 --> 16:09.480
We need to run!

16:09.700 --> 16:12.450
We need to run, or I'll be next!

16:12.740 --> 16:14.820
It's okay. Stay with us.

16:14.820 --> 16:15.960
We'll protect you.

16:15.960 --> 16:17.780
Where was the bear?

16:17.780 --> 16:19.080
Impossible!

16:19.080 --> 16:22.130
He's going to eat me! For sure!

16:22.130 --> 16:24.580
So get as far away from me as you can!

16:24.890 --> 16:26.100
What does that mean?

16:26.100 --> 16:29.300
Dad... Brother Jiro, Brother Taka...

16:29.300 --> 16:30.840
It ate them all!

16:31.110 --> 16:33.460
Mister Hood, come with me!

16:37.450 --> 16:40.610
And it ate Sister Noriko, too.

16:40.610 --> 16:42.380
It's my fault!

16:42.380 --> 16:45.450
I'm the one who brought the wenkamuy!

16:46.350 --> 16:51.230
Master Heita, who are these 
people you're talking about?

16:57.950 --> 16:59.990
Noriko, get back to the hut!

16:59.990 --> 17:04.000
Oh my, what an unusual group.

17:04.370 --> 17:06.750
Do you like my body?

17:09.810 --> 17:11.760
That thing at your feet...

17:12.740 --> 17:14.220
That's a bear pelt.

17:16.560 --> 17:18.470
When did that get here?

17:18.840 --> 17:23.480
"When"? You've been carrying it on your 
back like it was really important to you!

17:23.480 --> 17:26.460
No! I keep throwing it away!

17:26.460 --> 17:28.410
I burn it! I throw it in the river!

17:28.410 --> 17:31.230
And then the next thing I know 
I find myself holding it again!

17:31.460 --> 17:36.510
Do you think the bear that 
you two saw was that pelt?

17:38.360 --> 17:40.880
Hurry! Run!

17:41.230 --> 17:46.540
Maybe the wenkamuy that Heita's talking 
about only exists in his head.

17:51.340 --> 17:52.640
Master Heita!

17:52.640 --> 17:53.550
What's wrong?

18:05.760 --> 18:09.310
Matsuda Heita, one of the 
death row inmates at Abashiri.

18:10.570 --> 18:12.630
You wouldn't believe that guy.

18:12.630 --> 18:14.320
I remember him really well.

18:14.660 --> 18:18.820
This freak would change the way 
his voice sounded all the time.

18:19.130 --> 18:22.470
Once in a while, he'd try 
to sound like a sexy woman.

18:22.470 --> 18:24.290
It was disgusting.

18:24.760 --> 18:33.460
Once he told me something. That there 
were many other people inside him.

18:33.750 --> 18:35.920
And he was always scared of this brown bear

18:35.920 --> 18:39.440
he swore was stalking 
around outside the prison.

18:39.440 --> 18:41.720
It's there. It's right outside...

18:42.020 --> 18:44.790
The something-kamuy, he called it.

18:44.790 --> 18:47.350
Some kind of evil god 
that had eaten a person.

18:47.350 --> 18:48.850
The wenkamuy.

18:49.230 --> 18:50.290
Yeah, that's it.

18:50.290 --> 18:52.110
He said this wenkamuy was

18:52.110 --> 18:57.990
attacking and eating the people 
in his head, one after another.

18:58.530 --> 19:03.020
And in the end, the wenkamuy 
will eat me and take over.

19:03.020 --> 19:06.370
And when that happens I'll 
go to hunt someone...

19:06.370 --> 19:09.000
I'll have to kill them to make it stop.

19:09.820 --> 19:11.850
When I kill a person in the real world,

19:11.850 --> 19:16.300
my body explodes into pieces 
that fly all over the mountain.

19:16.300 --> 19:19.050
And then I go back to the old me.

19:19.310 --> 19:21.330
It happens again and again.

19:21.330 --> 19:23.450
Again and again...

19:24.430 --> 19:29.030
Where I'm from, when a wenkamuy is defeated, 
we don't take its meat or its pelt.

19:29.030 --> 19:31.940
We chop its body up into tiny pieces 
and scatter it all over the mountain.

19:31.940 --> 19:34.060
That must be what he was referring to.

19:34.600 --> 19:40.380
The wenkamuy is taking control of me, 
trying to get me to escape from the prison!

19:41.110 --> 19:42.490
Look at this!

19:42.490 --> 19:46.490
There're all these tattoos on my body, 
and I can't remember how they got here!

19:48.360 --> 19:52.280
You'd think it was all some bullshit 
story he came up with, right?

19:54.170 --> 19:57.800
But if you look at the records for the trial,

19:57.800 --> 19:59.970
he was found wearing the 
pelt of a brown bear,

19:59.970 --> 20:04.050
ripping apart the victim's body,
taking their flesh, and...

20:04.720 --> 20:07.420
Matsuda Heita, the Brown Bear Man.

20:07.420 --> 20:13.060
If what he said is true, he might be 
out there somewhere doing it again.

20:21.000 --> 20:22.080
Sugimoto!

20:27.070 --> 20:28.450
<i>He's so strong, it's inhuman!</i>

20:47.630 --> 20:51.050
Good! The wenkamuy is weakened!

20:52.890 --> 20:54.560
Now I can...

21:04.720 --> 21:06.700
Sugimoto, are you okay?

21:06.920 --> 21:08.310
I did it.

21:08.690 --> 21:10.450
I beat him...

21:12.830 --> 21:14.210
This is where we just were.

21:14.490 --> 21:19.210
I lured you here so he wouldn't notice.

21:19.510 --> 21:21.180
We need to get the poison arrow out!

21:21.180 --> 21:22.960
Asirpa-chan, do something!

21:23.600 --> 21:26.220
No, leave me.

21:26.710 --> 21:32.970
I was so scared of the story of the wenkamuy 
that I heard when I was a child...

21:32.970 --> 21:35.980
I always pictured in my head.

21:35.980 --> 21:39.530
I'd spend the whole day working 
myself to the bone digging gold...

21:39.530 --> 21:43.350
And my family would waste the 
money before the day was up.

21:43.350 --> 21:49.490
I wanted to punish them for how greedy 
they'd become over the gold.

21:49.870 --> 21:53.490
And one day I found an animal corpse 
that a bear was saving to eat for later.

21:53.880 --> 21:58.750
I took it home and hid 
it where everyone slept.

21:59.750 --> 22:03.510
It killed my family, but before
 it could eat me,

22:03.510 --> 22:07.580
an Ainu hunter slew it and its 
body was chopped into bits.

22:08.780 --> 22:13.730
After that, the wenkamuy came 
back to life again and again...

22:14.060 --> 22:17.640
To punish my family!

22:18.740 --> 22:22.810
And in the end, I was 
punished for my greed, too.

22:23.250 --> 22:28.910
I became a wenkamuy and went 
to attack an innocent person.

22:29.220 --> 22:31.840
I wanted someone to stop me.

22:31.840 --> 22:39.810
And because you fought the wenkamuy, 
Sugimoto-san, I can finally be rid of it.

22:47.800 --> 22:50.190
Where we live, it's said that

22:50.190 --> 22:56.220
people slain by a wenkamuy were taken 
away because the gods favored them.

22:56.600 --> 23:01.480
So wenkamuy don't kill people to punish them.

23:01.940 --> 23:05.890
I think he only heard part 
of the stories of the Ainu...

23:06.500 --> 23:10.490
which created a wenkamuy inside him 
that should have never existed.

23:10.920 --> 23:13.370
It's important to pass 
on the truth properly.

23:13.640 --> 23:17.160
So his lust for gold ruined his life?

23:18.020 --> 23:21.680
Or maybe there's something in 
gold that drives men mad.

23:23.630 --> 23:25.690
Don't die, Master Heita!

23:26.010 --> 23:28.380
Tell me where to dig next!

23:28.790 --> 23:32.160
Master Heita!

23:35.240 --> 23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Partner in Crime</b>

23:36.090 --> 23:39.160
Next time: "Partner in Crime"!
